Why AGPL-3.0
------------
Onshell.cloud is a tool people point at their own servers, using credentials
they cannot afford to have mishandled. That trust is only checkable if the code
running the service is the code you can read. The AGPL is what keeps those two
things equal: anyone who runs a modified version of this software as a network
service has to offer that version's source to its users, so a hosted Onshell can
never quietly diverge from this repository.

Trademarks
----------
The AGPL grants rights to the software, not to the name. "Onshell", the
Onshell.cloud name, the logo in docs/onshell_cloud_logo.png, and the brand assets
under apps/web/public/brand are not covered by the licence. You may run, fork,
and modify this code freely; if you offer it publicly, use your own name and
branding so nobody is misled about who is holding their credentials.

Third-party software
--------------------
This distribution depends on third-party packages, each under its own licence.
Run `yarn licenses list` for the resolved set. Notable runtime components:

  ssh2            (MIT)            SSH/SFTP client used by the gateway
  node-pty        (MIT)            pseudo-terminals for local and agent shells
  guacd / Apache Guacamole (Apache-2.0)  RDP protocol bridge, run as a service
  xterm.js        (MIT)            terminal renderer
  Fastify         (MIT)            API and gateway HTTP server
  Next.js         (MIT)            web application framework
  Electron        (MIT)            desktop application shell
  Prisma          (Apache-2.0)     database access layer
